<title>LATVIA: SHIPPING SELL-OFF CANDIDATES PLAN CONSORTIUM.</title>
<headline>SHIPPING SELL-OFF CANDIDATES PLAN CONSORTIUM.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some of the candidates for the privatisation of the Latvian Shipping Company have entered talks on forming a consortium, the Dienas bizness newspaper said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Latvian Shipping is estimated to be the world's 19th largest shipping firm and has 40 tankers, 24 refrigerated vessels and seven dry cargo vessels. Annual turnover is close to $300 million.</p>
<p>Around 14 companies have applied to participate in the privatisation, including the European Bank for Resonstruction and Development (EBRD), Lavinia Corporation, Sea Trade, and Britain's Tufton Oceanic, the newspaper writes.</p>
<p>A group of companies, set up by Nomura, Hansa Investment and Norway's Marsoft have also applied.</p>
<p>-- Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
